{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]There's a dark and a [C]troubled side of [G]life
[G]There's a bright, there's a sunny side, [D]too
Tho' we [D]meet with the darkness and [G]strife
The [D]sunny side we also may [G]view
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Keep on the sunny side, [C]always on the sunny [G]side
[G]Keep on the sunny side of [D]life
It will [G]help us every [G7]day, it will [C]brighten all the [G]way
[G]If we'll keep [C]on the [G]sunny [D7]side of [G]life
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The storm and its fury broke today
Crushing hopes that we cherish so dear
Clouds and storms will, in time, pass away
The sun again will shine bright and clear
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Let us greet with the song of hope each day
Tho the moment be cloudy or fair
Let us trust in our saviour always
Who keepeth everyone in his care
{end_of_chorus}
